cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Weft in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: Weft
abstract: >-
  Weft is a web application for comparing gene clusters. It aligns all proteins
  encoded in a set of annotated nucleotide records against each other and draws
  the result as an interactive multi-row gene map, with cross-record similarity
  shown as ribbons between genes.
authors:
  - given-names: Karol
    family-names: Ciuchciński
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0982-1377"
version: 1.0.0-rc2
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/kciuchcinski/weft"
keywords:
  - comparative genomics
  - gene clusters
  - synteny
  - protein alignment
  - visualization
